   "ruling": "Ruling: representation; project retained. For a Schedule D filer the helper is the smaller of Schedule D lines 15 and 16, floored at zero, plus Form 1040 line 3a, as i8995 p. 4, Line 12 says. When Schedule D is not required ('your net capital gain is the amount reported on Form 1040 ... line 7a') the only capital item in scope is capital gain distributions, and the Schedule D lines are still figured from line 13 alone, so lines 15 and 16 both equal the line 7a amount (checked earlier: $1,234 of distributions gives sd.line15 = sd.line16 = f1040.line7a = qbi.net_capital_gain = $1,234). No change to the data.",
   "subject_key": "11fbbdc340cf59b520e040c32b03f8b164d940ed2bc5345cc2a234930628f635"
